* ''Talk it out, then decide'' (operator, 2026-11-07: //"AIs often fall into a trap of holding a slot in the turn for 'only the operator can decide' items -> mu that, we talk it out, apply the mu tools, talk story over 2026/5492 user stories, and decide. only then do remaining uncertainties surface to the operator"//). Every fork weighs against the house laws by name: no global now, no backward compatibility in early alpha, causal islands, identity-as-relation, Infrastructure-as-Myth. The seat and every lead decide, name the fork and the reason, and surface only an uncertainty that survives the talk-out, with a default. Classifier refusals, destroy-class acts and the operator's own hands still surface at once.

